From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yue Gao <yuega2@cisco.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Oct 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: bonding: optional per-packet LAG hash override hook

SONiC Policy-Based Hashing computes a member-selection hash from a
rule-selected set of (possibly inner-header) fields at ingress, and needs
to hand that value to the bond TX path for a PortChannel next hop.

There is no existing channel for that. bond_tx_hash() materialises an
array of vlib_buffer_get_current(b) pointers and calls
bif->hash_func (ptd->data, h, n); the vnet_hash_fn_t signature is
void (*)(void **p, u32 *h, u32 n) -- no vlib_buffer_t, so a feature-arc
node upstream cannot communicate with it. Registering a new hash function
does not help either: bond_create_if() resolves hash_func by hard-coded
name string per bif->lb enum.

Unlike patch 0011, which adds a whole new hash *algorithm*, PBH needs an
*override* that keeps the configured algorithm as the fallback: only the
packets a PBH rule actually matched get a substituted hash.

The hook is deliberately payload-free. sonic_ext is an out-of-tree plugin
and vlib_buffer_t metadata is a shared, upstream-owned resource:
vnet_buffer_opaque2_t.unused[] and the VNET_BUFFER_F_AVAIL bits are a
common pool that upstream features consume over time, so a plugin that
takes a word or a bit from it has to re-litigate the claim at every uprev
and can collide with whoever claims it next. The plugin therefore keeps
its per-packet state in storage it owns outright, and this patch reduces
to a registration hook: one function pointer and one call site.
buffer.h is untouched, and so are bond.api and its CRC.

Properties:

  - NULL by default, so stock behaviour is byte-for-byte unchanged and
    the call site is a permanently predicted-false branch unless a plugin
    registers.
  - The guard is evaluated once per *frame*, not once per packet.
  - hash-eth-l34 and every other registered hash function still run and
    still produce h[]; the override only replaces selected entries.
  - No API, no ABI, no CRC change.

b is advanced by the gather loops, so the original base is saved as b0
and handed to the callback parallel to h[].

Signed-off-by: Yue Gao <yuega2@cisco.com>
---
--- a/src/vnet/bonding/node.h
+++ b/src/vnet/bonding/node.h
@@ -365,6 +365,15 @@
   u32 actor_state;
 } lacp_stats_t;

+/* Optional LAG-hash override.  The registered vnet_hash_fn_t is handed only
+   packet data pointers, so a feature that has already computed a per-packet
+   member-selection hash upstream has no channel by which to deliver it.  A
+   plugin may register here to substitute entries of h[] after the configured
+   hash function has run; NULL (the default) preserves stock behaviour
+   exactly.  b[] is the frame's buffer array, parallel to h[]. */
+typedef void (*bond_lag_hash_override_fn_t) (vlib_main_t *vm,
+					     vlib_buffer_t **b, u32 *h, u32 n);
+
 typedef struct
 {
   /* pool of bonding interfaces */
@@ -393,6 +402,9 @@
   bond_per_thread_data_t *per_thread_data;

   lacp_stats_t **stats;
+
+  /* see bond_lag_hash_override_fn_t */
+  bond_lag_hash_override_fn_t lag_hash_override;
 } bond_main_t;

 /* bond packet trace capture */
--- a/src/vnet/bonding/device.c
+++ b/src/vnet/bonding/device.c
@@ -207,6 +207,7 @@
 {
   u32 n_left_from = n_left;
   void **data;
+  vlib_buffer_t **b0 = b;

   ASSERT (bif->hash_func != 0);

@@ -240,6 +241,12 @@
     }

   bif->hash_func (ptd->data, h, n_left_from);
+
+  /* Let a registered plugin substitute per-packet hashes.  Inert unless
+     something registered: one predicted-false test per frame. */
+  if (PREDICT_FALSE (bond_main.lag_hash_override != 0))
+    bond_main.lag_hash_override (vm, b0, h, n_left_from);
+
   vec_reset_length (ptd->data);
 }

